[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4390926050","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119292#issuecomment-4390926050","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119292","id":4390926050,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBbg24g","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-06T18:40:52Z","updated_at":"2026-05-06T19:09:20Z","body":"This isn’t the only signal that returns `name`, so the “shadowing” issue between `Node prop “name”` vs `signal arg “name”` occurs in every other class as well. The solution is simply that users can arbitrarily change the signal’s argument name; it's already easy possible, and well-documented.\r\n\r\nThere’s no point in fixing only `AnimationPlayer`, and since this PR would likely cause a compatibility break on the `emit_signal(name = \"\")` on C# side, I believe this PR should not be merged.\r\n\r\nI am unsure whether we should introduce the concept of reserved words, but if we were to make such a change, I believe it should be addressed simultaneously with the property name consistency fixes in Godot 5.0.\r\n\r\nSeparate from this PR, you can send a PR to modify the arguments for the entire engine’s signals all at once and discuss it there. And it would be preferable to add a CI/CD check to prevent the use of “name” as a signal name like that checks for all shadowing by comparing the bound property name list with the signal argument list.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4390926050/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4391012579","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119292#issuecomment-4391012579","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119292","id":4391012579,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBbmI4w","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-06T18:54:49Z","updated_at":"2026-05-07T08:29:09Z","body":"> `emit_signal(name = \"\")` on C# side\r\n\r\n`emit_signal` is a vararg method so I'm not sure that is legal, there's no introspection available for signals or argument enforcement\r\n\r\nCC @raulsntos \r\n\r\nEdit: This is not a problem, see https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/89721#issuecomment-2014233366","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4391012579/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"outdated"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4391153030","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119292#issuecomment-4391153030","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119292","id":4391153030,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBbuthg","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-06T19:16:46Z","updated_at":"2026-05-06T19:41:41Z","body":"> This is not a problem, see https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/89721#issuecomment-2014233366\r\n\r\nIf there are no issues, I think the change can be accepted.\r\n\r\n> Separate from this PR, you can send a PR to modify the arguments for the entire engine’s signals all at once and discuss it there. And it would be preferable to add a CI/CD check to prevent the use of “name” as a signal name like that checks for all shadowing by comparing the bound property name list with the signal argument list.\r\n\r\nHowever, as I mentioned above, changing only the AnimationPlayer is meaningless (at least when it comes to animation-related classes, AnimationLibrary and AnimationNode should also be targets). Therefore, I suggest you send a new PR that applies the changes to the entire engine. This allows us to revert to a single commit if any problems occur by that. And as noted in the comments, it would be even better if you could detect and fix any shadowing issues other than the `name` field at the same time.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4391153030/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4394779946","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119292#issuecomment-4394779946","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119292","id":4394779946,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBfMFKg","user":{"login":"raulsntos","id":3903059,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDMwNTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3903059?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos","html_url":"https://github.com/raulsntos","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-07T06:51:55Z","updated_at":"2026-05-07T06:51:55Z","body":"> This is not a problem, see https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/89721#issuecomment-2014233366\r\n\r\nThat comment is a bit outdated, since 4.4 we now generate strongly-typed emit methods so changing parameter names in signals breaks source compatibility in C# just like it does for any regular method. Users could have this in their code: `EmitCurrentAnimationChanged(name: \"\")`.\r\n\r\nWe usually allow these breaks because we expect users will be able to fix them easily, and we don't expect named parameters to be used much although we don't have any numbers to back this up.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4394779946/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4400118912","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119292#issuecomment-4400118912","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119292","id":4400118912,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBkR8gA","user":{"login":"AtomicAntt","id":89709922,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5NzA5OTIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/89709922?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtomicAntt","html_url":"https://github.com/AtomicAntt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtomicAntt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtomicAntt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtomicAntt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtomicAntt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtomicAntt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtomicAntt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtomicAntt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtomicAntt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtomicAntt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-07T18:50:18Z","updated_at":"2026-05-07T18:50:18Z","body":"Thank you for the feedback! I have posted a new PR at https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119316 which addresses more of the shadowing issues from having the signal parameter be called `name` from what I have found.\r\n\r\nThe new PR also addresses `current_animation_changed(name: StringName)` from this PR.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4400118912/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]